        "kind": "pull_request",
        "title": "fix(config): reject schema-only keys",
        "body": "## What Problem This Solves\n\nTwo fields were still accepted by `openclaw.json` even though no runtime code consumed them:\n\n- `session.maintenance.rotateBytes`: the session-store rotation feature was removed, while the canonical schema/type/help surface kept advertising the retired key.\n- `gateway.remote.enabled`: remote mode is selected by `gateway.mode`; this second boolean had no reader and stale policy-coverage metadata claimed otherwise.\n\nAccepting no-op fields misleads operators and hides configuration mistakes.\n\n## Why This Change Was Made\n\nRemove both schema-only fields from the canonical Zod/type/help/metadata surfaces and add validation tests proving they are rejected as unknown. Keep the existing raw `openclaw doctor --fix` migration for `rotateBytes`, so older configs retain their supported repair path. Regenerate config baselines and align current docs with the rejection behavior.\n\n## User Impact\n\nConfigs containing either no-op key now fail validation instead of appearing to configure behavior. `openclaw doctor --fix` continues to remove legacy `session.maintenance.rotateBytes`; remote Gateway selection continues through `gateway.mode = \"remote\"`.\n\nRelease-note context: config validation now rejects the retired `session.maintenance.rotateBytes` and unused `gateway.remote.enabled` fields instead of silently accepting them.\n\n## Evidence\n\n- Blacksmith Testbox via Crabbox: focused config, doctor, help, store, and generated-baseline suite; 209 tests passed across 3 shards.\n- `pnpm config:docs:check`: passed.\n- `pnpm config:schema:check`: passed.\n- `pnpm policy:config-coverage`: passed; 210 monitored paths, no unclassified or unmatched paths.\n- `pnpm plugin-sdk:surface:check`: passed; 345 entrypoints and 11,219 exports.\n- `pnpm format:check -- <touched files>`: passed.\n- `git diff --check`: passed.\n- Fresh autoreview: no accepted/actionable findings.\n\n`pnpm check:changed` passed on Blacksmith Testbox `tbx_01kxcvfs91639fmq2s3bwge8cy`, including generated Plugin SDK API baseline, core/test typechecks, core/scripts lint, and repository guards. After an unrelated two-commit `main` advance, two fresh Testbox leases were shut down during hydration before commands ran; exact current head static fallback checks passed for config/API baselines, Policy coverage, Plugin SDK surface, TypeScript LOC ratchet, docs MDX, and diff whitespace. The remote test/full-gate proof is content-equivalent to the rebased patch.\n\nAI-assisted: yes.\n",
